# Ask the campus knowledge base, on /kb/query.
#
# Deterministic lookup over the structured dataset -- no embeddings, no vector
# store, no similarity search (CLAUDE.md). Runs entirely on the Pi, so this
# service answers identically whether or not the laptop is awake, which is the
# point of the info-desk role.

string query          # normalised or raw; the service normalises either way

# Where the asker is standing. Empty means the reception node where Neo lives,
# which is the right default for a desk robot and the only origin it will have
# until there is a body to move.
string origin_node
---
# The rendered answer, ready to speak. Produced by the template renderer, which
# is the primary output path and not a fallback -- when the link is up an LLM
# may re-phrase it, but it may not change a fact.
string answer

float32 confidence

# The four outcomes, kept distinct because they are four different sentences and
# collapsing them is how a robot starts inventing rooms (plan 7.2.6).
uint8 ANSWERED = 0
uint8 ROOM_UNKNOWN = 1          # block is surveyed, so the room really isn't there
uint8 BLOCK_NOT_SURVEYED = 2    # "I haven't learned C block yet" -- not the same thing
uint8 AMBIGUOUS = 3             # several candidates; ask a clarifying question
uint8 outcome

# True for ANSWERED and for the two honest misses -- this was an info-desk
# question and the KB owns it. False means "not my domain, try the LLM path",
# which is what the intent router branches on.
bool in_domain

# Candidate codes when outcome is AMBIGUOUS, so the caller can build the
# clarifying question ("CS-204 in B block, or CS-240 in C block?") without a
# second round trip.
string[] candidates
